{"data": [{"author_id": "2034728878636421120", "created_at": "2026-11-01T13:03:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116878724691828909"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/CNUrETCxor", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/nightraccai/status/2116878724691828909/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116878679410143232", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/CNUrETCxor"}]}, "id": "2116878724691828909", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 252, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"CLAUDE IS THE BEST AI\" AND \"GPT IS THE BEST AI\" ARE SEPARATED BY 0.8 POINTS.\n\nI pulled the actual leaderboard instead of the marketing slides.\n\nSWE-bench Verified, same harness for all three:\nClaude Opus 5 — 97.00%\nDeepSeek V4 Pro — 96.40%\nGPT-5.6 Sol — 96.20%\n\nThat's the whole https://t.co/CNUrETCxor", "url": "https://x.com/nightraccai/status/2116878724691828909"}, {"author_id": "894631624809345024", "created_at": "2026-10-31T12:09:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116502941607858485"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/krD2Rua8ej", "end": 233, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/nemui_nekoooo/status/2116502941607858485/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116502933609299968", "start": 210, "url": "https://t.co/krD2Rua8ej"}]}, "id": "2116502941607858485", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 350, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI's hardest tests don't last long:\n\nHumanity's Last Exam: 9% → 61% in 21 months ARC-AGI-2: 3% → 95% in 19 months ARC-AGI-3: 0.4% → 63% in 6 months\n\nEvery new \"impossible\" benchmark falls faster than the last. https://t.co/krD2Rua8ej", "url": "https://x.com/nemui_nekoooo/status/2116502941607858485"}, {"author_id": "1923609574210191360", "created_at": "2026-10-31T16:06:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116562354196681093"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Mhbhzrt86d", "end": 249, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/CraigMLdsouza/status/2116562354196681093/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116561871629086720", "start": 226, "url": "https://t.co/Mhbhzrt86d"}]}, "id": "2116562354196681093", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 33, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Benchmark Teardown #4: Where did the money go?\n\nI analyzed 855 coding-agent runs on SWE-bench Verified: 19 model + agent configurations, 45 shared tasks, one run each, and $1,449 in logged spend.\n\nHere’s where the runs went 👇 https://t.co/Mhbhzrt86d", "url": "https://x.com/CraigMLdsouza/status/2116562354196681093"}, {"author_id": "1478336800980713472", "created_at": "2026-11-01T09:59:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116832609720287442"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 123, "start": 116, "tag": "Claude"}, {"end": 162, "start": 155, "tag": "Gemini"}, {"end": 186, "start": 178, "tag": "ChatGPT"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/jZJZTtu8uv", "end": 292, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SPetryha/status/2116832609720287442/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116832601763692544", "start": 269, "url": "https://t.co/jZJZTtu8uv"}]}, "id": "2116832609720287442", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Everyone’s arguing which AI is «smarter.» The actual numbers tell a more specific story.\n     • IQ-style benchmark: #Claude Sonnet 5 scores 145 (perfect), #Gemini 129, Grok 126, #ChatGPT 121 — a 24-point spread between top and bottom\n      • Hallucination rate: Claude https://t.co/jZJZTtu8uv", "url": "https://x.com/SPetryha/status/2116832609720287442"}, {"author_id": "2109046651298205696", "created_at": "2026-10-31T15:54:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116559545233441062"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 220, "id": "1714438092655149056", "start": 212, "username": "ChatGPT"}, {"end": 241, "id": "84107004", "start": 234, "username": "Claude"}, {"end": 265, "id": "1720665183188922368", "start": 260, "username": "grok"}]}, "id": "2116559545233441062", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Happy Halloween, fellow sci-fi enthusiasts! 🎃\n\nHere’s a scary question: who’s closest to AGI: artificial general intelligence: GPT, Claude, or Grok?\n\nBest reported scores on the ARC-AGI-2 reasoning benchmark:\n\n• @ChatGPT Astra: 95%\n• @Claude Opus 5.5: 93.3%\n• @Grok 4.7: 61.4%", "url": "https://x.com/AshMaddoxWrites/status/2116559545233441062"}, {"author_id": "1832056619120910336", "created_at": "2026-11-01T16:35:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116932172787384689"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/claudeai/statu…", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/claudeai/status/2116220869479428500", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/73tUIAmT8e"}]}, "id": "2116932172787384689", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 85, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116220869479428500", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The usage-limit war reaches Claude: Anthropic renamed Max 20x to Ultra and is removing the 5-hour limit for verified Ultra accounts. Ultra stays $200, Max 5x becomes plain Max at $100, and weekly limits don't change.\n\nThe pricing page now lists Ultra as 10x Pro every week, which https://t.co/73tUIAmT8e", "url": "https://x.com/cm2cDrON7V3956/status/2116932172787384689"}, {"author_id": "2793483243", "created_at": "2026-11-01T00:52:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116694904089038971"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/jnpTvANaTK", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/nothingto12/status/2116694904089038971/video/1", "media_key": "13_2116694864628703232", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/jnpTvANaTK"}]}, "id": "2116694904089038971", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 3111, "like_count": 27, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 LOVES to cheat! It searched online for answers on 390 of 1200 SWE-bench tasks!\n\nRound 4: Postmortem Part 2\n\nSame model, 4 providers, 300 tasks each. I went through every run and found it taking shortcuts: searching for answers and/or the tests that https://t.co/jnpTvANaTK", "url": "https://x.com/nothingto12/status/2116694904089038971"}, {"author_id": "269786915", "created_at": "2026-11-01T10:27:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116839439292895587"], "id": "2116839439292895587", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 46, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A Turing Award winner's lab beats GPT-6 and Opus at proving what can't be done. \nAn AI agent explores games it has never seen, works out their rules and then proves mathematically when a goal is impossible. On two unwinnable levels it produced machine-checked impossibility proofs", "url": "https://x.com/szilagyipal/status/2116839439292895587"}, {"author_id": "1471115361600737282", "created_at": "2026-11-01T01:26:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116703470686269846"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/qPdJ9nXCSs", "end": 293, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/h___t____n/status/2116703470686269846/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116703441288417280", "start": 270, "url": "https://t.co/qPdJ9nXCSs"}]}, "id": "2116703470686269846", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Coding agents re-learn your repo every session, and you pay for it. Microsoft Research and UC Berkeley's TokenEconomizer says it cuts that waste by 18.4–30.9%. 💸\n\nIt works with Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot CLI and Pi without changing the agent itself, using three https://t.co/qPdJ9nXCSs", "url": "https://x.com/h___t____n/status/2116703470686269846"}, {"author_id": "4141032860", "created_at": "2026-11-01T05:17:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116761466288447810"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/XZW9MVcpoY", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/madhugogineni97/status/2116761466288447810/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116761454066139136", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/XZW9MVcpoY"}]}, "id": "2116761466288447810", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 322, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI Updates - 1 Nov 2026 🤖\n\nKimi K3.1 Pro's full weights are coming by Nov 4, with a 1M token context. Moonshot says its hallucination rate fell from 23% to under 7% on a hard internal test.\nNot gonna lie, open-weight models haven't excited me lately. That hallucination number https://t.co/XZW9MVcpoY", "url": "https://x.com/madhugogineni97/status/2116761466288447810"}, {"article": {"title": "Benchmark test scores for Gemini Carbon + KUT 19 module with the KUT Code Agent harness integrated"}, "author_id": "995612364232798209", "created_at": "2026-11-01T09:05:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116818936323080341"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2116…", "end": 234, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116808389317763072", "start": 211, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116808389317763072", "url": "https://t.co/8wQvSqTH5e"}]}, "id": "2116818936323080341", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3272, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "This is a comprehensive record covering the development, verification, and establishment of an operational foundation for a software development automation system, spanning all 19 modules of **KUT Code Agent**. https://t.co/8wQvSqTH5e", "url": "https://x.com/MLB_Connection/status/2116818936323080341"}, {"author_id": "1738513411799920640", "created_at": "2026-11-01T10:07:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116834406807593230"], "id": "2116834406807593230", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 443, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Sunday is here! You are awakening from a post-Halloween slumber that turned a Trojan scare into an Ohio State horror! Ouch! College football has become a prediction engine designed specifically to humiliate predictions. Before this weekend, the AP had already counted 10 top-10", "url": "https://x.com/SulkaMike/status/2116834406807593230"}, {"article": {"title": "The Slopsquatting Trap: How Autonomous Coding Agents Weaponize Phantom Dependencies"}, "author_id": "67694456", "created_at": "2026-10-31T20:15:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116625152721227845"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2116…", "end": 270, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116621558114643968", "start": 247, "status": 404, "unwound_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116621558114643968", "url": "https://t.co/1i8tyP4ItU"}]}, "id": "2116625152721227845", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 579, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "LLMs hallucinate phantom packages in 18% of code.\n\nNow attackers pre-register those names on PyPI with malware. When your coding agent hits ModuleNotFoundError and runs `pip install`, you just gave them root.\n\nThe Slopsquatting Trap, and the fix: https://t.co/1i8tyP4ItU", "url": "https://x.com/PatchOnChain/status/2116625152721227845"}, {"article": {"title": "Intelligence That Compounds Through Experience"}, "author_id": "2040374346158682112", "created_at": "2026-10-31T19:52:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116619411453010303"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/article/2116…", "end": 155, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/i/article/2116600330314297344", "start": 132